  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>A mass–spring system oscillates on a frictionless horizontal surface with simple harmonic motion. The mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> oscillates with angular frequency <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\omega\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The total energy is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{T}=\\frac{1}{2}m\\omega^{2}x_{0}^{2}\"></span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{0}\"></span> is the maximum displacement.</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Show that <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{T}\"></span> can be written as <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{T}=\\frac{1}{2}kx_{0}^{2}\"></span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"k\"></span> is the spring constant. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> </p><p>Calculate the maximum elastic potential energy of this system.</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"k=24.5 N m^{-1}\"></span></p><p>[1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong> </p><p>In a second trial, the mass is doubled, and the spring is compressed by the same amount as before.</p>\n<p>Determine <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\textit{maximum speed of the mass in the first trial}}{\\textit{maximum speed of the mass in the second trial}}\"></span>.</p><p>[2]</p></section>"
  },
